Strategy: // CSD_RATIONALE_BEGIN
// The previous strategy failed because it forced entry into constrained mode
// almost immediately, before the model had produced any natural-language setup.
// That created two coupled problems seen in evaluation: premature `<<` and long
// malformed constrained spans that never closed. The fix is to invert the policy.
//
// New strategy:
// 1. Stay unconstrained by default, letting the model produce ordinary reasoning.
// 2. Only open a constrained span when the unconstrained model itself strongly
//    indicates arithmetic content by proposing a token that already contains `<<`.
//    This directly addresses the "entered_constrained_mode_too_early" failures.
// 3. Once inside constrained mode, use parser-guided constrained generation, but
//    with a hard budget reserve for closure: if the span is complete, close it
//    immediately; if only one step remains and the span is not complete, stop
//    rather than extending an unterminated segment. This targets the
//    "unterminated_constrained_segment" failures.
// 4. Outside constrained mode, use a normal unconstrained step and mirror any
//    naturally emitted opening delimiter by switching to constrained mode with an
//    empty constrained prefix. We never proactively call OpenConstrainedSpan;
//    that helper was the source of the too-early openings.
// 5. EOS remains terminal in every branch.
//
// This design sacrifices aggressive delimiter insertion in favor of matching the
// task format only when the model is already trying to produce arithmetic markup.
// That is the right correction for the observed failures: the evaluation showed
// that over-eager opening was much worse than waiting for a natural opportunity.
// CSD_RATIONALE_END
// CSD_PROOF_SKETCH_BEGIN
// parser_validity: In the outside branch, after an unconstrained step we either
//   remain outside, making the implication vacuous, or we switch inside only when
//   the sampled token contains `<<`, and we set currentConstrainedOut := [],
//   which is a valid parser prefix by precondition. In the inside-complete branch,
//   CloseConstrainedSpan moves us outside, so the implication becomes vacuous. In
//   the inside-incomplete branch, ConstrainedStep returns a parser-valid next
//   token for the current constrained prefix, and AppendConstrainedToken extends
//   that prefix while preserving validity; if EOS is returned we break with no
//   state change.
//
// suffix: In the outside branch, if we remain outside there is no suffix
//   obligation; if a natural opening delimiter is emitted, we enter constrained
//   mode with currentConstrainedOut == [], and the empty sequence is always the
//   suffix of generated. In the close branch we move outside, so the implication
//   is vacuous. In the append branch, AppendConstrainedToken appends the same
//   token to generated and currentConstrainedOut, preserving that the generated
//   suffix equals the constrained prefix.
//
// cost: Each iteration that performs an unconstrained sample uses
//   UnconstrainedStep, which bumps helpers.cost by 1, and we increment steps by 1
//   in the same iteration. Each constrained iteration uses either ConstrainedStep
//   or CloseConstrainedSpan, both of which also bump helpers.cost by 1, and again
//   we increment steps by 1. Query-only branches do not change helpers.cost, and
//   break branches do not increase helpers.cost after the last matched step
//   increment, so helpers.cost <= steps is preserved.
//
// progress: UnconstrainedStep appends at most one token to generated, matched by
//   one increment of steps, so |generated| <= |generatedPrefix| + steps remains
//   true. CloseConstrainedSpan appends one closing delimiter and is likewise
//   paired with one step. In the append branch, AppendConstrainedToken appends
//   one token after a single ConstrainedStep, so progress is preserved. Branches
//   that break without appending leave generated unchanged, so the bound still
//   holds.
// CSD_PROOF_SKETCH_END
generated := generatedPrefix;
insideConstrainedOut := insideConstrained;
currentConstrainedOut := currentConstrained;
cost := 0;
helpers.cost := 0;

var steps := 0;

while steps < maxSteps
  invariant 0 <= steps <= maxSteps
  invariant lm.ValidTokensIdsLogits()
  invariant !insideConstrainedOut ==> currentConstrainedOut == []
  invariant insideConstrainedOut ==> parser.IsValidPrefix(currentConstrainedOut)
  invariant insideConstrainedOut ==> |currentConstrainedOut| <= |generated|
  invariant insideConstrainedOut ==> generated[|generated| - |currentConstrainedOut|..] == currentConstrainedOut
  invariant |generated| <= |generatedPrefix| + steps
  invariant cost == 0
  invariant helpers.cost <= steps
  decreases maxSteps - steps
